WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.208 --> 00:00:03.458
We can’t sit at home waiting 
for news about adoptions.

00:00:03.458 --> 00:00:04.458
Ahh. 
What?

00:00:04.458 --> 00:00:05.541
We’re never gonna find a kid.

00:00:05.541 --> 00:00:06.708
They go so quickly.

00:00:06.708 --> 00:00:07.625
This is you.

00:00:07.625 --> 00:00:08.000
What?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.083
You took too long again.

00:00:09.083 --> 00:00:11.791
Yeah, but it’s difficult choosing 
a child from a photograph,

00:00:11.791 --> 00:00:14.500
isn’t it? You wanna get in there 
and kick the tires a little bit. 

00:00:15.958 --> 00:00:17.041
Are you set on a girl?

00:00:17.041 --> 00:00:19.375
Girls tell you what they're feeling. 
They know how to ask for help.

00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:22.166
You just sit on a sofa hugging a 
cushion, sighing louder and louder 

00:00:22.166 --> 00:00:23.541
until someone asks 
you what’s wrong.

00:00:23.541 --> 00:00:25.333
Boys are uncomplicated.

00:00:25.541 --> 00:00:26.250
You alright then?

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.041
Yeah... yeah...

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.125
You?

00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:34.083
Yeah... yeah...

00:00:37.541 --> 00:00:40.125
What is the one thing that we 
need to be able to take these kids?

00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:42.291
Money, experience,

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:43.500
preparation.

00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:44.875
I know it’s hard.

00:00:44.875 --> 00:00:46.250
It’s a mammoth 
undertaking

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:46.958
and I should know 

00:00:46.958 --> 00:00:49.708
I brought up two happy, 
friendly, well-adjusted children

00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:51.083
out of four.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.125
Please, I’m having enough 
trouble getting my own family

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.750
without keeping your 
one functioning too.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.875
Okay fine. We need to 
talk about childcare.

00:01:02.875 --> 00:01:04.375
I’ve been babysitting. 

00:01:04.375 --> 00:01:05.875
It’s not even called 
that when they're yours.

00:01:07.958 --> 00:01:09.541
Just don’t let them 
be fussy eaters. 

00:01:09.541 --> 00:01:12.041
My friend Clayton only ate 
toast until he was twelve

00:01:12.041 --> 00:01:13.708
and now he’s 
really into S&amp;M.

00:01:13.958 --> 00:01:14.666
Has this helped?

00:01:14.666 --> 00:01:15.416
Massively.

00:01:16.416 --> 00:01:17.791
What if it changes things?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:18.708
Whatever happens,

00:01:19.291 --> 00:01:20.583
we'll be messing 
things up together.

00:01:21.666 --> 00:01:23.208
You don’t want to 
meet at this stage.

00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:24.333
It could jeopardize
the adoption.

00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:26.791
Just pretend you’re visiting the 
school on professional business. 

00:01:26.916 --> 00:01:28.875
If we’re being other people, 
should we do accents? 

00:01:28.875 --> 00:01:30.083
I can do American.

00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:30.583
Show me.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.583
Well howdy partner.

00:01:32.583 --> 00:01:34.000
I’m going to stop you right there. 
It’s absolutely perfect.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:40.833
What?

00:01:40.916 --> 00:01:42.083
On your last visit 
to the school,

00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:43.958
did you happen to see a 
strange American woman

00:01:44.458 --> 00:01:45.291
bothering the children?

00:01:45.291 --> 00:01:45.875
What?

00:01:45.875 --> 00:01:46.250
No.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:47.166
Oh my goodness.

00:01:47.166 --> 00:01:49.583
Yeah look, she says lovely to see 
you both and I’ll be in touch soon.

00:01:49.583 --> 00:01:51.791
Don't do that!

